# Chaos: Ok on the death window logs in again after the connection timed out (modules/game_playerdeath/playerdeath.lua,
# modules/client_entergame/characterlist.lua; after 0001-0216; client/BASE.md "0217"). Seen in a client 2026-11-27 (V38,
# three times): the death window stayed open 30 s or longer, the client ended the game and showed "Connection timed out
# ... (ERROR 110)"; Ok did nothing because it called CharacterList.doLogin() only while online. Cause: the server removes
# a dead player at once and sends that connection nothing more, so the client's 30 s read timeout ends the game.
#  * playerdeath.lua: onGameEnd keeps an open death window (one event later it takes the input lock back from the
#    character list); onGameStart closes it (any relog, auto reconnect included); Ok calls CharacterList.doLogin()
#    unless a login is already running (LoginEvent:tryLogin logs in at once when offline, logs out first when online);
#    Cancel while offline leaves the character list showing. holdsConnectionError() is true while the window is open.
#  * characterlist.lua: onGameConnectionError asks game_playerdeath.holdsConnectionError() first and shows no error box
#    for the expected end of a dead player's session.
# The first hunk spans the whole death module file, so client/tools/death_relog_patch_test.py runs the old and the new
# file on a fake engine.
